 function referenceHtml(){return `<div class="panel-title"><span>MECHANICS REFERENCE</span><em>CANON · INTERPRETATION · IMPLEMENTATION</em></div><div class="reference-grid"><article class="reference-card"><h3>Canon anchors</h3><p>The entry sequence references the Cruxtruder, Totem Lathe, Alchemiter, Kernelsprite, and Cruxite artifact. Prospit and Derse are the two dream moons. Lands, Consorts, Denizens, Gates, prototyping, and server/client assistance are represented as session concepts; this console does not simulate the full story mechanics.</p></article><article class="reference-card"><h3>Interpretations</h3><p>Class and Aspect descriptions are thematic guides, not exhaustive definitions or personality predictions. Land motifs, quest connections, NPC knowledge, and Denizen trials are generated creative material, not definitive canon mechanics.</p></article><article class="reference-card"><h3>Implementation rules</h3><p>Seeded assignment, uniqueness controls, one connected server tree with one initial host, topological entry order, and seven sequential Gate states are application rules. Prototype records identify available, planned, and completed influences; only applied completed influences are active. Meteor times are estimates, not live timers. No combat, economy, or online multiplayer is implemented.</p></article><article class="reference-card"><h3>Data & persistence</h3><p>Validation checks Classpect constraints, the server/client graph and entry order, player-owned Lands and sprites, seven distinct registered Gate locations and route states, prototype statuses, and Consort NPC details. Save stores one local browser copy; Export JSON downloads portable session data. Imported files are validated before activation.</p></article></div>${validationHtml()}`}
